# Google Maps browser key — used by the map page (Maps JS SDK, Places
# Autocomplete) and by the geocoder that turns a device fix into a street
# address.
#
# This is a PUBLIC_ variable: it is inlined into the client bundle and is
# readable by anyone using the app. That is inherent to a browser key, and the
# way you protect it is restriction, not secrecy — in the Google Cloud console,
# limit the key to the Maps JavaScript, Places, and Geocoding APIs, and to the
# bmltsearch.bmlt.app HTTP referrer plus the iOS/Android bundle IDs.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own key. CI reads it from the
# GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY repository secret.
PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_KEY=
